   "subject": "Re: line type not respected when saving to jpg?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div>A simple example works fine for me.</div><div><br></div><div>df &lt;- data.frame(x=1:3, y=1:3)</div><div>p &lt;- ggplot(df, aes(x, y)) + geom_path()</div><div>p2 &lt;- ggplot(df, aes(x, y)) + geom_path(lty=2)</div><div><br></div><div><div>ggsave((&quot;~/Desktop/hello.jpg&quot;), p)</div><div>ggsave((&quot;~/Desktop/hello2.jpg&quot;), p2)</div><div>ggsave((&quot;~/Desktop/hello.png&quot;), p)</div><div>ggsave((&quot;~/Desktop/hello2.png&quot;), p2)</div><div><br></div><div>Perhaps there is a bug, in using polar coordinates or something like that, but without MWEs (see the instructions at the bottom of the email), it is hard to tell. </div><div><br></div><div>Best wishes,</div><div>Doug</div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div>\r\n<br><div></div></div>"
    ],
